    "cross_field_rules": [
      "Strict JSON: reject duplicate keys, nonstandard numeric constants, invalid UTF-8 and missing or unknown fields.",
      "Exact version and canonical schema digest in workspace and independently retained registry.",
      "Exact context equality across workspace, registry, basis records, previous.captured_for and operations; calendar-valid canonical UTC as_of.",
      "candidate_release_id is separate from context and equal in registry and operations; context.release_id is forbidden.",
      "Exactly one root of each fixed kind; unique root IDs and exact required root membership.",
      "Root owner/read_roles/write_roles exactly match root_policy; fixture declarations never create runtime authority.",
      "Canonical absolute lexical paths, no dot/parent/empty components, backslash aliases or trailing dots/spaces; Windows additionally rejects UNC/device/ADS/reserved names and compares case-insensitively.",
      "Every root is disjoint from every other root: no equal path or ancestor/descendant overlap.",
      "Only PLAIN_DECLARATION alias observations are accepted; actual symlink/reparse/hardlink/TOCTOU proof remains a native provider obligation.",
      "Relative operation paths cannot escape roots; unknown roots and operation IDs duplicated in one plan are rejected.",
      "Every operation must satisfy fixed role access. CURRENT access is forbidden throughout preparation, including D4 calls.",
      "Candidate operations bind the exact candidate release/snapshot/as_of tuple; previous operations require explicit PRESENT previous and its independent tuple.",
      "Non-generation source/configuration/capture/sealed operations require generation=null with NOT_APPLICABLE; unknown generation is not NOT_APPLICABLE.",
      "Previous NOT_VERIFIED has null identity/evidence and an explicit reason; null identity never implies ABSENT.",
      "Previous ABSENT requires explicit retained PREVIOUS_ABSENCE basis. PRESENT requires retained matching PREVIOUS_CONTENT and independent release/snapshot IDs.",
      "as_of, acquisition and coverage bases are separately resolved by ID, kind and context; acquisition time never supplies business as_of and actual membership never supplies independent coverage.",
      "SYNTHETIC_ONLY basis requires a reference and no reason; NOT_VERIFIED requires null values with explicit NOT_VERIFIED reason. No official VERIFIED status is accepted by this synthetic contract.",
      "A prepared candidate can only be PREPARED/NOT_ATTEMPTED; publication and CURRENT verification belong to separate providers and contracts."
    ],
